{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"Profiling shows the fused attention program itself now dominates (about 54% of GPU time), because its six small matrix products use scalar-quality IEEE FP32. The Q/K/V inputs are BF16 values exactly representable in FP16, and the final Q/K/V gradients are already FP16, so I’m moving those inner products to CDNA4’s FP16 matrix cores and measuring the resulting error carefully."}}
