{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"agent_message","text":"The unified hidden GEMM preserves full numerical margin locally and lowers that path from roughly 95 μs to 26–37 μs. One final opportunity remains: the four 1280×1280 weight gradients are all transposed token reductions. I’m testing a single batched Triton kernel for them, which can remove the last hidden-state conversion and both large output casts."}}
